1
00:00:12,640 --> 00:00:13,640
(Let it go.)

2
00:00:44,220 --> 00:00:46,000
=Revenge From A Wife=

3
00:00:46,820 --> 00:00:48,320
=Episode 6=

4
00:00:51,200 --> 00:00:52,039
Wanniang.

5
00:00:53,320 --> 00:00:54,840
You're a good-hearted person.

6
00:00:55,719 --> 00:00:57,200
Let me say a little more.

7
00:00:57,880 --> 00:00:59,159
I know you can't let this go.

8
00:00:59,679 --> 00:01:01,039
But you're no match for her.

9
00:01:01,520 --> 00:01:03,240
After the late Empress died of illness,

10
00:01:04,159 --> 00:01:05,840
Noble Lady Chen entered the palace.

11
00:01:06,799 --> 00:01:08,479
She quickly rose above the rest,

12
00:01:09,479 --> 00:01:10,920
became His Majesty's favorite,

13
00:01:11,400 --> 00:01:12,599
and was soon made a consort.

14
00:01:13,359 --> 00:01:14,920
Consort Chen is so overbearing

15
00:01:15,879 --> 00:01:18,560
not just because she's
the late Empress's younger sister.

16
00:01:19,200 --> 00:01:20,840
Her uncle, Zhang Heng,

17
00:01:21,079 --> 00:01:23,400
wields immense power as
the Marquis of the Northern Frontier.

18
00:01:24,040 --> 00:01:25,719
You and I are but blades of grass.

19
00:01:26,439 --> 00:01:27,760
We can't beat her.

20
00:01:28,359 --> 00:01:29,439
Even a mighty dike can collapse

21
00:01:29,959 --> 00:01:31,120
from the tiniest breach.

22
00:01:31,959 --> 00:01:32,840
Cattails may be frail,

23
00:01:33,280 --> 00:01:34,359
but fire can't destroy them,

24
00:01:35,079 --> 00:01:36,680
and they will rise again with the wind.

25
00:01:36,920 --> 00:01:38,040
The way you are,

26
00:01:38,480 --> 00:01:40,799
you really do resemble the late Empress.

27
00:01:41,400 --> 00:01:42,640
You seem gentle,

28
00:01:43,159 --> 00:01:44,319
but you're stubborn underneath.

29
00:01:44,799 --> 00:01:45,680
Once you make up your mind,

30
00:01:46,239 --> 00:01:47,319
you never turn back.

31
00:01:49,120 --> 00:01:49,879
Very well.

32
00:01:50,079 --> 00:01:51,519
I'll tell you

33
00:01:52,000 --> 00:01:53,159
everything I know.

34
00:01:53,840 --> 00:01:54,799
(That day,)

35
00:01:55,159 --> 00:01:57,599
(Nanny Liu told me everything)

36
00:01:57,959 --> 00:01:59,200
(about the late Empress
and His Majesty,)

37
00:01:59,480 --> 00:02:00,760
(one story at a time.)

38
00:02:05,000 --> 00:02:05,920
Thank you, sir.

39
00:02:09,079 --> 00:02:10,200
My surname is Gu.

40
00:02:10,599 --> 00:02:12,120
I'm a traveling merchant from the north.

41
00:02:13,519 --> 00:02:15,599
I hear you're well-versed in medicine.

42
00:02:15,960 --> 00:02:16,879
I've come seeking a remedy.

43
00:02:18,719 --> 00:02:19,479
Have a seat.

44
00:02:29,800 --> 00:02:32,280
Have you had trouble sleeping for long?

45
00:02:32,879 --> 00:02:33,560
That's right.

46
00:02:34,159 --> 00:02:35,599
What do you think is causing it?

47
00:02:35,599 --> 00:02:37,479
May I see your tongue?

48
00:02:52,879 --> 00:02:54,039
(Nanny Liu told me)

49
00:02:54,800 --> 00:02:55,960
(I didn't need to imitate her exactly.)

50
00:02:56,800 --> 00:02:58,800
(I only needed to resemble her halfway.)

51
00:02:59,879 --> 00:03:01,439
(His Majesty would fill in the rest)

52
00:03:01,439 --> 00:03:03,360
(with the image he longed to see.)

53
00:03:22,759 --> 00:03:23,879
These herbs still hold moisture.

54
00:03:24,159 --> 00:03:25,319
They can flare up near fire.

55
00:03:26,000 --> 00:03:27,080
Please stand back.

56
00:03:33,120 --> 00:03:33,599
Thank you.

57
00:03:35,479 --> 00:03:36,439
May I ask,

58
00:03:37,319 --> 00:03:38,000
this illness of mine...

59
00:03:38,639 --> 00:03:39,719
how would you treat it?

60
00:03:39,960 --> 00:03:41,319
Your pulse

61
00:03:41,599 --> 00:03:42,520
is neither shallow nor rapid.

62
00:03:42,879 --> 00:03:44,280
It suggests unresolved grief

63
00:03:44,280 --> 00:03:45,159
that's built up over time.

64
00:03:45,840 --> 00:03:47,000
In other words,

65
00:03:47,319 --> 00:03:48,199
your illness

66
00:03:48,759 --> 00:03:49,719
doesn't come from the body,

67
00:03:50,360 --> 00:03:51,439
but from the heart.

68
00:03:53,039 --> 00:03:54,919
A troubled heart is hardest to heal.

69
00:03:55,479 --> 00:03:56,560
Ordinary medicine

70
00:03:56,800 --> 00:03:57,680
can ease symptoms, not the cause.

71
00:03:58,360 --> 00:03:59,120
However,

72
00:03:59,400 --> 00:04:00,599
I may know a way

73
00:04:01,080 --> 00:04:02,840
that could cure what ails you.

74
00:04:04,719 --> 00:04:05,639
What is it?

75
00:04:06,759 --> 00:04:08,280
If you trust me,

76
00:04:08,560 --> 00:04:09,960
come back after I close at dusk.

77
00:04:10,719 --> 00:04:11,919
I'll take you somewhere.

78
00:04:12,919 --> 00:04:13,360
All right.

79
00:04:17,599 --> 00:04:18,439
I'll get back to work.

80
00:04:35,759 --> 00:04:36,319
Let's go.

81
00:04:51,720 --> 00:04:52,680
The herb you mentioned...

82
00:04:53,480 --> 00:04:54,519
it grows somewhere like this?

83
00:04:55,199 --> 00:04:57,160
Yours isn't an ordinary illness.

84
00:04:57,439 --> 00:04:58,800
So ordinary medicine won't do.

85
00:04:59,480 --> 00:05:00,000
Let's go.

86
00:05:08,000 --> 00:05:09,240
Looks like you're

87
00:05:09,480 --> 00:05:11,560
just a pretty face, Mr. Gu.

88
00:05:11,920 --> 00:05:12,600
How dare you...

89
00:05:16,000 --> 00:05:17,000
talk to me like that?

90
00:05:17,360 --> 00:05:18,439
You're so touchy.

91
00:05:18,959 --> 00:05:19,879
Get up here,

92
00:05:20,079 --> 00:05:21,720
or I'll leave you here for the bugs.

93
00:05:34,879 --> 00:05:35,720
Careful!

94
00:05:55,530 --> 00:05:57,373
♪Who calls from deep within old dreams♪

95
00:05:57,860 --> 00:05:59,860
♪So softly♪

96
00:06:03,600 --> 00:06:05,380
♪I hear you in the wind♪

97
00:06:05,506 --> 00:06:09,020
♪Sighing softly♪

98
00:06:11,853 --> 00:06:13,800
♪I've searched far and wide♪

99
00:06:16,000 --> 00:06:16,480
Don't move.

100
00:06:20,493 --> 00:06:22,330
♪Where the lights flicker♪

101
00:06:22,440 --> 00:06:25,613
♪Old dreams drift like smoke♪

102
00:06:27,400 --> 00:06:29,690
♪I don't want to wake from this dream♪

103
00:06:29,760 --> 00:06:31,770
♪I don't want this love to end♪

104
00:06:31,893 --> 00:06:33,840
♪No mountain or sea can stop♪

105
00:06:33,906 --> 00:06:35,800
♪My heart from longing for you♪

106
00:06:35,866 --> 00:06:38,020
♪Life itself is but a shadow♪

107
00:06:38,133 --> 00:06:42,770
♪Love and hate both come to nothing♪

108
00:06:43,946 --> 00:06:46,010
♪Old dreams remain beyond my grasp♪

109
00:06:46,340 --> 00:06:48,080
♪I can't let go of this love♪

110
00:06:48,199 --> 00:06:48,680
Look.

111
00:06:48,920 --> 00:06:49,720
This is a vine blossom.

112
00:06:50,240 --> 00:06:51,399
It grows only in bamboo groves.

113
00:06:51,839 --> 00:06:52,879
Its scent is gentle

114
00:06:53,160 --> 00:06:54,000
and calms the mind.

115
00:06:56,360 --> 00:06:56,920
Let's go.

116
00:06:57,079 --> 00:06:57,800
It's getting dark.

117
00:07:05,920 --> 00:07:06,600
Mr. Gu.

118
00:07:07,000 --> 00:07:07,879
Come on up!

119
00:07:17,240 --> 00:07:19,186
♪I don't want to wake from this dream♪

120
00:07:19,440 --> 00:07:21,213
♪I don't want this love to end♪

121
00:07:35,983 --> 00:07:39,570
♪Sunset fades beyond the lonely city♪

122
00:07:40,290 --> 00:07:43,900
♪Dusk snow paints the green hills♪

123
00:07:44,183 --> 00:07:46,330
♪A lone rider storms the old pass♪

124
00:07:46,700 --> 00:07:48,343
♪Drunk, I gaze by lamplight♪

125
00:07:48,830 --> 00:07:52,970
♪Old friends have all drifted away♪

126
00:07:53,356 --> 00:07:56,970
♪My broken sword rusts, as do I♪

127
00:07:57,476 --> 00:08:01,180
♪Jackdaws cry into the night♪

128
00:08:01,503 --> 00:08:03,590
♪Half a banner snaps in the wind♪

129
00:08:04,196 --> 00:08:06,050
♪In dreams, I return to the camps♪

130
00:08:06,410 --> 00:08:10,210
♪Moonlight chills my armor♪

131
00:08:10,516 --> 00:08:14,860
♪Life is a dream through many winters♪

132
00:08:15,130 --> 00:08:18,860
♪I gaze beyond the edge of the world♪

133
00:08:18,970 --> 00:08:21,370
♪Parting sorrow spills across the moon♪

134
00:08:21,750 --> 00:08:27,076
♪The moon and wind mean nothing now♪

135
00:08:27,570 --> 00:08:30,470
♪History turns to ash before ink dries♪

136
00:08:30,530 --> 00:08:36,460
♪Who plays the zither
and sighs at the pavilion?♪

137
00:08:36,710 --> 00:08:40,970
♪The past has faded away♪

138
00:08:40,970 --> 00:08:46,970
♪The past has faded away♪
